<item>
<title>Acast acquires Backyard Ventures</title>
<link>https://podnews.net/update/acast-bv</link>
<pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 10:30:41 +0000</pubDate>
<podcast:transcript url="https://podnews.net/audio/podnews260812.mp3.vtt" type="text/vtt" rel="captions"/>
<description><![CDATA[They paid $20mn for the company, which has audiences of more than 230 million every month.

Sponsored by Magellan AI. Find out where Q2 podcast ad dollars went, live with Magellan AI on August 20. Sign up for the webinar <a href="https://podnews.net/cc/3645">https://podnews.net/cc/3645</a>

Visit <a href="https://podnews.net/update/acast-bv">https://podnews.net/update/acast-bv</a> for the story links in full, and to get our daily newsletter.]]></description>
<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><i>Sponsored by <strong>Magellan AI</strong>. Find out where Q2 podcast ad dollars went, live with Magellan AI on August 20. <a class="l" style="font-weight:bold;color:#BC1515" href="https://podnews.net/class-click/3645/2026-08-12">Sign up for the webinar</a></i></p><ul>
<li>Podcast marketplace <a href="https://podnews.net/press-release/acast-acquires-backyard-ventures">Acast has acquired Backyard Ventures</a>, a US-based podcast network, for US $20mn. Backyard Ventures is home to podcasts like Piers Morgan's Uncensored, Ryan Holiday's The Daily Stoic, and audiences of more than 230 million. The team from Backyard Ventures will stay with the business; the brand will be retired as the company is integrated into Acast. Backyard shows are currently hosted and monetised by ART19 and Megaphone.</li>
<li><a href="https://podnews.net/press-release/podcast-consultant-rise25">The Podcast Consultant has acquired B2B podcasting service Rise25</a>. Rise25 co-founder Dr Jeremy Weisz becomes The Podcast Consultant's Director of Client Success. No terms were given.</li>
<li><a href="https://newsroom.spotify.com/2026-08-11/equal-podcast-audiobook-ambassadors/?utm_source=podnews.net&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=podnews.net%3A2026-08-12">Spotify has announced its first EQUAL Ambassador for podcasts</a>, Morgan Absher, to help amplify and celebrate women podcast creators. Podnews covered the story last week; our sister publication <a href="https://podcastbusinessjournal.com/interviews/morgan-absher/?utm_source=podnews.net&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=podnews.net%3A2026-08-12"><em>Podcast Business Journal</em> has a full interview.</a></li>
